_I answered by email but also answering here for visibility._
​
​Mocking the request when there is no query should work.

```ts
const algoliaClient = algoliasearch(
  "latency",
  "6be0576ff61c053d5f9a3225e2a90f76"
);

const searchClient = {
  search(requests) {
    if (requests.every(({ params }) => !params.query)) {
      return Promise.resolve({
        results: requests.map(() => ({
          hits: [],
          nbHits: 0,
          processingTimeMS: 0,
        })),
      });
    }

    return algoliaClient.search(requests);
  },
};
```

If you only want the very first empty query to be skipped, you can add a boolean flag to ignore the check for the next searches.​
